From 265c7777320bb06b492ce4d55241e1100314d384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Wu <a2wujinyuan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:47:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Silicon/Qualcomm: GeniSerialPortLib: Fix polling for set bits

GeniSerialPollBit() compares the masked register value with the BOOLEAN
it waits for, so waiting for a bit to become set only succeeds for bit 0.
SerialPortRead() waits for GENI_M_SEC_IRQ_EN (bit 31) and for a non-zero
RX FIFO word count this way. The first never matches, so every character
read runs into the full 10 ms timeout, and the console drops input that
arrives faster than 100 characters per second, a pasted line for
instance.

Compare whether the bit is set instead. Waiting for bits to clear keeps
working as before.
---
 Silicon/Qualcomm/Library/GeniSerialPortLib/GeniSerialPortLib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Silicon/Qualcomm/Library/GeniSerialPortLib/GeniSerialPortLib.c b/Silicon/Qualcomm/Library/GeniSerialPortLib/GeniSerialPortLib.c
index d041597763..c4cc2ba48e 100644
--- a/Silicon/Qualcomm/Library/GeniSerialPortLib/GeniSerialPortLib.c
+++ b/Silicon/Qualcomm/Library/GeniSerialPortLib/GeniSerialPortLib.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ GeniSerialPollBit (
   TimeOutUs = 10000;
 
   do {
-    if ((MmioRead32 (Reg) & Bit) == Set) {
+    if (((MmioRead32 (Reg) & Bit) != 0) == Set) {
       break;
     }
 
